{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790888572,"nonce":"eT7vZO9WRtAKpN7HMKZ0kJY8HD4=","title":"A Finding cannot be seen or asked for in the UI, so an Investigation exists only through the API","message":"**What is wrong.** `180a525` stores Investigations, Steps and Findings; case detail shows none of them and has no \"Investigate\" action. ADR 0016 requires the UI to render a snapshot as \"what was seen at T\", never as live state.\n\n**Where.** `web/src/routes/case-detail.tsx`: an Investigate action, the latest Finding with its timestamp and Investigator version, an expandable Step transcript, tokens spent, and `exhausted`/`skipped` states shown as such.\n\n**Scope.** small.\n\n**Done when.** A user requests an Investigation from case detail and sees its Finding labelled with the time it was reached; Steps are browsable; exhausted and skipped runs are visibly so; component tests cover each state; `tsc` green.\n\n**Blocked by.** `180a525`\n\n**Mode.** AFK — can be implemented and merged without a human decision. Source: ADR 0052/0053/0054 design session, 2026-10-02.","files":null}]}